edits_description = "The people and stalls were cut out to be used in a composition."
blurb = "Like the rest of the series, this print depicts famous theatrical characters comically reimagined at a market.

The vendor in the top right of the image sells fruit. Although today fruit is usually called kudamono (\"fruit thing\"), in the Edo period it was called mizugashi (水菓子, \"water sweets\"), to distinguish naturally sweet, watery fruits from manufactured confectioneries."
